# netsurf: counters across a local build (patch 374)
# Generated 2026-11-06
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 373)
#
# Box construction numbers CSS counters in one flat table per build pass
# (fixes134b), so a subtree built alone counts from an empty table. 369's
# table restyle declined on any "counter-" in page CSS, and 372/373 on any
# counter() shown -- which, by the r98 census, is now what stops rte's
# carousel tracks and wpblog's and github's changes. The line path (165)
# never checked: a span::before showing counter() inside a paragraph read
# from an empty table after the paragraph's text changed.
#
# A local build only goes wrong when the rebuilt subtree itself takes part
# in counting. So:
#  - box_construct.c: every touch of the counter table (a reset, an
#    increment, a counter() shown) marks the counting element's parent box
#    VB_COUNTS (box.h, bit 22) and sets a flag box_counters_touched()
#    reads. The mark goes on the parent: the element being built has no
#    box_for_node of its own yet -- the one it returns there is the
#    replaced tree's, in a local build already freed. (A display:none
#    element counts nothing in this engine.)
#  - html.c, html_rl_box_counts(): an element box takes part in counting
#    if it or a box below it is VB_COUNTS, or its own style or its
#    ::before / ::after's style resets or increments a counter, or a
#    pseudo-element of it shows one.
#  - Each local builder declines a subtree that takes part in counting,
#    before freeing it, and hands a build that touched counters to the
#    full reconvert: the block restyle (174, and 373's route), 372's flex
#    restyle, 369's table restyle (html_rl_page_counters goes) and the
#    line path. html_rl_page_counter_shown (373) goes.
#
#  - Objects (found by the r99 scorecard: rte crashed, 2 of 2, once its
#    carousel tracks reached the flex rebuild). Every fetched object --
#    an <img>, and also a CSS background image, whose box->background is
#    set only when it arrives -- keeps o->box, which its load callback and
#    the full reconvert's html_reconvert_relink_objects read. No local
#    path ever checked for backgrounds: freeing such a box left the entry
#    dangling (a latent use-after-free since patch 165, rarely fatal while
#    the freed memory went unused). html_rl_objects_point_into() walks
#    each entry's box up to the subtree about to be freed; the line path,
#    the block, flex and table restyles, and removed blocks and floats
#    decline on it. html_rl_drop_new(): a build that gave up after it
#    fetched objects keeps its new boxes for the full reconvert instead of
#    freeing them (the entries point at them); the line path then keeps
#    its new children and frees the old line.
#
# Result on a 2500-paragraph sim page that shows a counter (median of 3):
# a flex track's style 108 -> 19 ms; text under ::before 104 -> 19 ms; a
# table cell's class 107 -> 18 ms.
#
